From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] adbd: ask LuneOS's developer mode service about unknown hosts

adbd 35 leaves the question whether to let a host in to libadbd_auth,
which on Android talks to the system server's AdbDebuggingManager:
it sends "CK", "DC", "WE" and "WF" packets that LuneOS's developer mode
service does not know. That service answers on the protocol adbd 5.1.1
used: adbd sends "PK<key> <user@host>" and reads "OK" or "NO".

This libadbd_auth, in place of upstream's, speaks that protocol:

- /run/adbd/auth is made by adbd itself (there is no Android init to
  pass a socket in), 0600 in a directory only root may enter (0700,
  checked and mended through one O_NOFOLLOW fd). Connections from anyone
  but root are closed (SO_PEERCRED). The newest connection is the
  service; one that restarted is asked the open question again.
- One question at a time, at most 16 hosts waiting. Every connection of
  the same key gets the user's answer to it.
- No answer within 75 s (the service's own limit is 60 s), or no
  service at all, refuses the host. An answer that arrives later, or
  after the host went, is never taken for the next question's: the
  service is disconnected then.
- Only a host's key is sent: a 2048-bit adb RSA key and a comment
  without control characters; anything else is refused unasked.
- Saved keys are read from /var/lib/adbd/adb_keys, which the service
  writes. The file has to be a regular file owned by adbd's user that
  nobody else may write, of at most 1 MiB, and is not followed if it is
  a link. Lines that are not keys are skipped with a log line each.
  Keys are logged by fingerprint only.

adbd's own auth.cpp checks the signature against those keys with
BoringSSL; the 5.1.1 fix for a mincrypt RSA_verify() that went to
OpenSSL's function of that name is not needed here.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: replaces libadbd_auth for the LuneOS developer mode service]
---
 debian/system/adbd.mk                         |   3 +-
 .../libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp       | 780 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.h  |  50 ++
 3 files changed, 832 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp
 create mode 100644 frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.h

diff --git a/debian/system/adbd.mk b/debian/system/adbd.mk
index a3f88f1..6431a36 100644
--- a/debian/system/adbd.mk
+++ b/debian/system/adbd.mk
@@ -42,7 +42,8 @@ LIBADBD_fs_SRC_FILES := \
 LIBDIAGNOSE_USB_SRC_FILES = diagnose_usb/diagnose_usb.cpp
 LIBASYNCIO_SRC_FILES = libasyncio/AsyncIO.cpp
 
-LIBADBD_AUTH_SRC_FILES = libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth.cpp
+# LuneOS: adbd asks org.webosports.service.devmode, not Android's framework.
+LIBADBD_AUTH_SRC_FILES = libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp
 
 LOCAL_SRC_FILES := \
   $(ADBD_SRC_FILES) \
diff --git a/frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp b/frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9fd79cd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/frameworks/native/libs/adbd_auth/adbd_auth_luneos.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,780 @@
